<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Woolworths completes MTN issue-Westpac.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Woolworths completes MTN issue-Westpac.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westpac Banking Corp said on Friday retailer Woolworths Ltd's first issue of A$100 million of 10-year unrated medium term notes (MTN) had been successfully completed.  </p>
<p>Investors were given the choice of fixed or floating rate notes, with many opting for the floating rate paper, Westpac said.</p>
<p>The floating rate notes were issued at a margin of 0.45 percentage points over the three month BBSW rate (Bank Bill Swap rate) while the fixed rate bonds were issued at a spread of 0.72 percentage points over the October 2007 government bonds.</p>
<p>The placement was underwritten jointly by Westpac and AMP and was taken up by six institutions.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
